WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.567
If you want to

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.534
gauge the real

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.402
state of our union,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.637
look no further than your kitchen table.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.505
At least that's according

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.141
to House Speaker Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.310
Inflation has exploded

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.746
Mortgage rates have doubled

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.148
working Americans after inflation

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.450
and taxes have gotten a pay cut.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.953
And AIG's

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.188
a staple of America's breakfast,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:25.291
have gone from a cheap source of protein

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.194
to a luxury. Good.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.329
If you're eating your eggs right

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:29.896
now, yes,

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.998
you know, the cost of eggs is up.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:32.432
In fact,

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.700
it's more than double

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.468
what it was just a year ago.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.237
So what are House

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.405
Republicans doing about it?

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.240
They are holding a series of high

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.609
profile hearings to get to the bottom of,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.744
well, not the price of eggs.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.046
Let's put it that way.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.546
Thank God

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.447
for Elon Musk

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.783
for allowing to show us in the world

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.051
that Twitter was basically

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.620
a subsidiary of the FBI.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.021
I want to assure you both here

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:58.258
we come not to trash the FBI,

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.560
but to rescue the FBI

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.695
from political capture.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.763
So I'll ask again,

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.331
did you shadow be on my account?

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.233
Yes or no?

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:07.500
Again,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.902
not to the best of my recollection.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.037
So the answer is, Mr. Roth. Yes, you did.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.441
So this is the committee

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.842
that's looking into the,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.142
quote,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.646
weaponization of the federal government,

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:20.914
federal government.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.682
And a Washington Post ABC

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.751
News poll asked a very simple question.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.453
What do you think about this committee?

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.487
Is it legitimate?

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.956
Is an attempt to score political points?

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.558
It's not even close.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.960
56% say it's an attempt to score

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.727
political points.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.162
And I come back to the point

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.398
that I often raise, which is that

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.500
voters are not as stupid

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.501
as people in Washington

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.602
seem to think that they are.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.170
They understand what's going on here.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:44.871
Well, yes.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.640
I mean, it's pretty plain insight

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.776
and not the first time that Congress

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.044
has formed a committee

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.879
to just have a political purpose,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:53.213
no doubt.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.115
But the American people are hip to it.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.216
I mean, listen,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.083
this is part

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.818
we were talking in the last segment

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.186
about Joe Biden's

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.621
good week on economic populism

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.255
or what have you.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:02.755
The other

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.224
part of the equation

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.625
is just the contrast

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.393
with what Republicans are doing.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.161
And so

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.130
that also is working to the president's

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:10.597
benefit right now,

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.731
because when the Republican House

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.600
majority fresh off,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.368
it's yes, more limited victory

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.836
perhaps than anticipated

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.605
puts this front and center

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.840
as as issue number one, not only do

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.509
the American people clearly see it

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.277
as political gamesmanship,

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.779
it is it is so far away

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.648
from the actual things

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.583
that the American people care about.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.684
That it means the Republicans

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.919
going to have to sort of make up ground

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.853
here as they go forward.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:35.855
That's right.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.956
I talked to

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.957
a representative comer

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.526
who is over the oversight committee

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.793
and I asked him,

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.194
you know,

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:41.928
a lot of Americans

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.196
are going to deem these hearings

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.731
as retaliation politics.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.965
And do you feel that way?

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.100
Are you going to do anything about it?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.468
And he said

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.636
they make no apologies

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.271
for making this part of their strategy.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.438
They believe investigating

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.673
the president is important

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.341
and bringing in issues

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.043
related to his family members.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.511
So to your point,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.913
I feel it's really striking,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.014
you know, as a Capitol Hill

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.115
reporter to see them

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.449
double down on this,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.884
knowing that the American people

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.119
aren't really interested,

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.654
knowing that over on the other side

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.421
of the Capitol,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.223
senators are doing hearings

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.491
on the Chinese

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.392
surveillance balloon

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.092
and other matters

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:13.860
that Americans really

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.528
want to tune in about.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.729
But right now,

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.331
what we're seeing is Republicans

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.400
off to a little bit of a slower start

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.634
on some of their plans,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.102
but yet they're not backing down.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.404
Yeah, I mean, it's

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.472
it is a little too transparent

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.642
and it also is so it's in such contrast

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.177
to when there's real work

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.378
being done to the real work

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.279
that's being done

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.480
in other parts of the Hill.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.416
One of the highlights

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.518
we'll call it a highlight of this week's

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.352
hearings

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.787
was conservatives

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.388
trying to make this claim

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.525
that social media was censoring them

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.993
due to undue influence

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.628
from people in the government.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:51.030
Just take a listen to this exchange

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.765
that happened between Congressman

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.101
Maxwell Frost and one of the Twitter

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:56.936
witnesses.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.371
In this hearing

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:01.841
earlier, you testified about a 2019 tweet

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.577
that was about President Trump.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.779
And I think it's from Miss Teagan.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.780
What was the tweet about?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.015
Please excuse my language.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.016
This is a direct quote.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.017
But Chrissy Teigen

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.185
referred to Donald Trump

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:15.555
as a free speech.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.190
And what happened after MS.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.491
Teigen posted her tweet?

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.759
What did the White House do?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.394
What did the Trump White House do,

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.729
for my understanding?

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:23.363
The White House

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.731
reached out to ask

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:27.600
that this tweet be removed.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.036
So this is all totally backfired

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.971
in spectacular fashion.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.675
I mean, it was one part of

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:38.678
I remember talking to a someone close

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.747
to President Biden, and they were

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:41.814
I was asking them

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.449
about the increased oversight

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.118
that would happen from Congress.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.053
And what they were saying is, look,

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.421
as long as we can

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.223
keep proposing plans

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.292
and frame the opposition

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.360
as not being pragmatic,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.396
but not getting things done,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.531
then that's going to be our strategy

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.966
going forward.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.234
This helps with that.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.069
This does help with that in a way.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.071
That being said, to say that

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.005
there's not people

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.206
that are nervous in the White House

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.474
about some of the increased

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.676
investigations,

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.611
including maybe on immigration

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.745
and potentially

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.280
the Homeland Security Secretary

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.048
being brought down.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.082
I wrote a story

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.850
this week about

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.885
White House officials

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.586
increasingly anxious

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.521
about the time

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.022
that it takes away

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.657
from actually addressing

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.926
real issues that are happening, I think.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.162
But I think that they've hired lawyers

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.029
to deal with it.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:30.496
But this is

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.431
I mean, the social media stuff

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:34.100
is such a cul de sac in all of this.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.337
I do want to get one more thing in here

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.138
on a bit of a different topic.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:39.739
Sarah Huckabee

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:40.740
Sanders

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.275
gave the Republican response

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.910
to Biden this week.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.178
And I just want to play real quick what

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:45.878
she had to say.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.614
Most Americans simply want

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.117
to live their lives in freedom and peace.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.786
But we are under attack in a left

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:54.821
wing culture war.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:55.888
We didn't start

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:58.224
and never wanted to fight.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:58.958
Every day

00:05:58.958 --> 00:05:59.592
we are told

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.494
we must partake in their rituals,

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:02.995
salute their flags

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:06.299
and worship their false idols.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:09.001
I it's it just speaks to this question

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:09.702
of what

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.471
path is the Republican Party

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:12.972
going to take here?

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:15.775
They seem to be leaning into the culture

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:17.643
war stuff in addition to all of this

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.411
sort of fringy

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.746
conspiracy stuff

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:21.547
on the social media platform.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:22.749
These are appeals

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.083
to the base

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.051
Pew Research Center,

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.352
which is really unparalleled,

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.787
has terrific

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:29.822
mainstream, large sample research

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:31.858
just in the last couple of days,

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.291
put out

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.026
an updated list of America's

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.162
top policy priorities

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.463
strengthen the economy.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.231
No. One.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:41.000
75% say it's top priority number

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.668
to reducing health care costs.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.603
That's why you see Biden

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.004
leaning into insulin

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.506
and some of these other discussions.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.975
Number three, defend against terrorism.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.510
That's why the border

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.577
and the China

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:54.247
spy plane issues have such resonance.

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.115
You got to get way down that

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.784
list to get to two issues

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.521
issues of race equity in America.

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.289
That's 32%.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.590
That would be on the Democratic base.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.491
Side, I think.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.026
And the issue of parents

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.494
having more control over things

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.762
or parental issues

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.130
down at 27%,

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.398
the only major issue

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:13.433
with lower interest in

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:16.569
that is COVID Here we are in early 2020.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.771
What about these are

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:19.772
these are issues

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.574
that really appeal to the base

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:22.542
when you're looking at

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.744
what's left of the center or swing voters

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:27.180
or the broadest base of Americans,

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.347
it's the economy.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.582
It's health care.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.249
It's it's

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.084
protecting American national security.

